course: dictionary
lesson: 3873
title: Fraud and scams
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Fraud is a word you will meet in safety lessons and stories. It means tricking people to get money or things in a dishonest way. «Banks use AI to spot unusual spending and block possible fraud» tells you that banks are trying to stop tricks like this.
explain: A fraud can also be a person. A fraud is someone who pretends to be someone or something they are not. A fraud can be a trick or a fake thing too, so you must be careful.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. In «A bank statement lists everything that went in and out of an account, and grown-ups check it for mistakes and fraud», the words bank, account and mistakes tell you fraud is about cheating people out of money. Try your meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense? Then you know.
explain: Sometimes a real payment gets blocked by mistake, so a bank's fraud check is useful but not perfect. If you are ever unsure about a message asking for money or your bank details, stop and ask a grown-up.
fact: Fraud means tricking people to get money or things dishonestly.
fact: A fraud is a person who pretends to be someone they are not.
fact: A fraud can also be a trick or a fake.
fact: Credit card fraud means someone uses your card to take money without your permission.
fact: Fake emails, phone calls and websites are common scams, so never give your bank details to someone who contacts you out of the blue.
exercise: «Banks use AI to spot unusual spending and block possible fraud.» What is fraud in this sentence? | *Tricking people to get money dishonestly | A bird that lives near banks | A happy surprise from the bank | A kind of bank statement
exercise: A fake email asks you to send your password to win a prize. What is this email? | A fast way to save money | *A scam, a trick to take your money | A helpful gift from your bank | A bank statement
exercise: Someone phones you and pretends to be a police officer to get your money. What is that person? | A friendly neighbour | A bank manager | A postman | *A fraud
test: What does «credit card fraud» mean? | A bank giving you a free card | *Someone using your card to take money without permission | A shop that sells cards | A card with a picture on it
test: Which word in the sentence «Food gained by fraud tastes sweet» is the trick word? | Gained | Sweet | Food | *Fraud
exam: «Food gained by fraud tastes sweet, but one ends up with a mouth full of gravel.» Which word means cheating people to get money or things? | *Fraud | Sweet | Food | Gravel
